menu "Firmgen Telemetry"

    config FG_TELEMETRY_TEMP_SENSOR
        bool "Sample on-chip temperature sensor"
        default n
        depends on SOC_TEMP_SENSOR_SUPPORTED
        help
            Reads the internal temperature sensor each interval and includes
            a "health":{"temp_c":...} field in the JSON output (shown as
            "CPU Temp" in the RTOS panel).

            OFF by default: enabling it makes the component require the
            esp_driver_tsens driver, which would otherwise be pulled into
            projects that don't use it. Turn this on only when you want the
            CPU temperature reading. Also disable it if your application
            already installs the temperature sensor driver — ESP-IDF allows
            only one owner of that driver at a time.

    config FG_PROTO_MONITOR
        bool "Enable protocol bus monitor"
        default y
        help
            Enables the firmgen_proto_monitor component. Call
            firmgen_proto_monitor_start() from app_main and use
            fg_proto_i2c() / fg_proto_spi() / fg_proto_uart() /
            fg_proto_wifi_rssi() / fg_proto_mqtt_pub() from your driver
            callbacks to log protocol activity to the Live Intelligence Panel.

endmenu
